Package: letools
Title: Life Tables and Demographic Decomposition for Population Health Metrics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jing-Zhong", "Wang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "jzwang1011@gmail.com")
Description: Construction of abridged life tables from age-specific mortality
    rates, with Kannisto or Gompertz extrapolation of old-age mortality,
    Coale-Demeny separation factors in infancy, and optional Keyfitz refinement
    elsewhere. Provides exact Arriaga and Pollard decompositions of differences
    in life expectancy, by age and by cause of death, and Chiang standard errors
    for life tables built from registered deaths. All functions operate
    column-wise over a matrix of posterior draws, so a single life table is the
    one-column case and uncertainty propagates without changes to calling code.
